[#:seon.task{:name "a-context-only-branch-read-is-not-supplied"
             :kind :function
             :intent "8871a5f77 made `:seon.store/store` and `:seon.agent/routing` world members, and its regression covers one-argument calls (a request plus the supplied context), but `my.agent/branches` takes only `:my.agent/branch-context`, so its documented call (`my.agent/branches`) has zero arguments and still refuses its argument count on default running fd293bdd7, which includes 8871a5f77 (2026-09-28, flow-processes-opus, root agent via MCP: \"expected a declared argument count (1), got an argument count of 0\"). Done when the zero-argument call answers my branch and the roster through the one path: the armed wrapper supplies a wholly omitted map argument whose declared schema's members are all world members, and the regression is that call from an agent's evaluation."
             :must-read #{my.agent/branches seon.call-preparation/preparing}}
 #:seon.task{:name "retire-branch-refuses-a-finished-agent-as-admission-closed"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`my.agent/retire-branch!` answered \"run transition refused: admission-closed\" for a finished probe agent (commit-floor lane, 2026-09-28): its branch agent-c67543ede734 stayed in the roster, so a finished agent cannot retire its own branch. The refusal comes from seon.turn's transition check (turn.clj:322-323, `:seon.agent/admission-closed-tx`) and reaches the agent as an error string; seon.mcp answers admission-closed as a bare one-key map (mcp.clj:178-186), not the one error shape. Done when retiring the branch of an agent whose admission is closed succeeds through `my.agent/retire-branch!` (branch unlinked, roster entry retired), the refusal for a genuinely running agent is the one error value naming the rule and the fix, a regression retires a finished agent from its own evaluation, and a retired agent's branch is also unlinked at run exit (the Flow launcher or seon.await) so agents need not call it."
             :must-read #{my.agent/retire-branch! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! seon.mcp/jvm-run}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/commit-floor--report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-retire-leaves-the-agent-admission-closed",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "`(my.agent/retire-branch! {:seon.store/branch :agent-cfd70b5547f7})` run by agent r-turn (default, 2026-10-07) refused 'branch :agent-cfd70b5547f7 still has a connection in this process; release its connection, then retire it.' AFTER closing admission on the hosted agent r-turn-a (tx 536872981). r-turn-a's own `(my.agent/retire-branch! ...)` then answered MCP with a bare '{`:seon.error/message` \"run transition refused: admission-closed\"}' (no type, no operation). The refusal must leave nothing changed (decide before closing admission), the hosted agent's connection release must be reachable from the caller, and the admission-closed refusal must be a typed error map. Proof: a deftest retiring a branch whose connection is held asserts the agent stays admitted.",
            :must-read #{my.agent/retire-branch!},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-turn-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "retiring-a-branch-allocates-a-hundred-megabytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root retiring twelve idle probe-agent branches in one sci evaluation, (my.agent/retire-branch! {:seon.store/branch b}) for each, allocated 1,333.8 MB in 11,737 armed calls and 655 ms (default pid 79558, e3b7bae3a, 2026-10-08, lane heap-leak): about 110 MB and 980 calls per retire, for agents that had each run a few trivial passes. Retirement stops one graph, releases one connection and unlinks one branch; that work should be proportional to the agent's live handles, not to the program or the store. Find the allocating owner with (seon.profile/measure (fn [] (my.agent/retire-branch! {:seon.store/branch b}))) and remove what it does that is proportional to more. Done when one retire of an idle agent's branch allocates under 5 MB, measured by that probe."
             :must-read #{my.agent/retire-branch! seon.cluster.agent/release-context! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "settings-root-writes-on-main-never-reach-an-agent-on-its-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root's (seon.agent/settings! {:seon.config.ai/no-provider false :seon.config.run/max-episode-runs 5} main-connection \"live-flash-2\") wrote the agent's overrides on main, but the agent works on its branch, whose turn reads its own copy of the agent entity: the branch kept {} (no-provider true from the cluster), so root's wake opened only a system turn and no model pass, while a message root sent landed on the agent's branch (live-agent run 2, default ade6e3059, 2026-10-08). The overrides took effect only when written through the agent's own MCP REPL (my.agent/settings!), an outside row in its history. Run 3 (default 0de932400, 2026-10-08): root's (seon.agent/settings! {...} (seon.db/branch-connection main-db :agent-6ea18cf66f12) \"live-flash-3b\") from root's JVM REPL refuses :seon.db.write/validation-refusal (\"names branch :agent-6ea18cf66f12, which is not the writing cluster's branch :cluster-default\"), so root has no route; the agent's own MCP REPL is still the only one. Agent information lives on the agent: done when the dials root sets for an agent are the ones the agent's pass reads, whichever branch it holds."
             :must-read #{my.agent/settings! seon.agent/settings! seon.agent/settings}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-read-as-another-agent-blocks-its-retirement"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Lane repl-only-2 (default 35e95e7b3, 2026-10-09) evaluated `(my.program/diff)` as agent a5-io through eval_clj to read its candidate: the request ran that branch's whole red test step (10.4 s of an 11.4 s request, 471 MB allocated) and the next read-only request (`my.program/declaration-diff` plus `source`) passed the bridge's 32 s bound with unknown outcome. Afterwards `(my.agent/retire-branch! {:seon.store/branch :agent-354d0c12bc21})` refused: the branch \"still has a connection in this process; release its connection, then retire it\", naming no call that releases it, although the docstring says retirement releases a hosted agent's execution itself. Done when another agent's declarations can be read without running as it (a diff of a named branch), and retire-branch! releases a connection only reads opened, or names the call that does."
             :must-read #{my.agent/retire-branch! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! my.program/diff}}]
